 filter part number is FC100A1037, with dimensions of 20 inches by 25 inches by 4 inches.", "The filter is a pleated design rated MERV 11, described in listings as an Ultra Efficiency Air Cleaning Filter.", "Available options include single units and 2-pack bundles, some of which feature same-day supply filter change reminders."]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO devices (brand_id, model_name, slug, category, seed_keyword, official_filter_code, hepa_grade, filter_shape, dimensions_json, compatibility_warning, faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json, status) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM brands WHERE slug = 'honeywell'), '4 Box', 'honeywell-4-box-replacement-filter', 'air_purifier', 'honeywell 4 filter box', 'FC100A1003', NULL, NULL, '{"length_in": 16, "width_in": 20, "height_in": 4}', 'Verify the exact model number on your Honeywell 4‑Box unit before ordering, as some listings (e.g., FC100A1037) reference larger 20 × 25 × 4‑inch filters that will not fit.', '[{"q": "What is the correct part number for a replacement filter for the Honeywell 4‑Box?", "a": "The official Honeywell part code listed for the 4‑Box filter is FC100A1003."}, {"q": "Are OEM Honeywell filters different from third‑party multi‑pack options?", "a": "OEM filters are branded Honeywell and sold as genuine replacements, while third‑party packs are compatible alternatives that may lack the OEM label but share the same dimensions."}, {"q": "What filtration level do the listed filters provide?", "a": "The titles do not specify a MERV rating, but they are described as pleated air filters; the exact filtration grade is not stated in the listings."}]', 'Replacement filters for the Honeywell 4‑Box air purifier use the official part code FC100A1003. While the exact MERV rating is not specified in the listings, both genuine Honeywell OEM packs and third‑party multi‑pack options are available, providing the standard 16 × 20 × 4‑inch dimensions for reliable replacement today.', '["Official Honeywell 4‑Box filter part code is FC100A1003 with a 16 × 20 × 4‑inch rectangular size.", "Listings show no explicit MERV rating, but filters are pleated and compatible with the 4‑Box unit.", "Buyers can choose genuine OEM single packs or value multi‑pack third‑party replacements."]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO devices (brand_id, model_name, slug, category, seed_keyword, official_filter_code, hepa_grade, filter_shape, dimensions_json, compatibility_warning, faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json, status) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM brands WHERE slug = 'honeywell'), 'Air Genius 5', 'honeywell-air-genius-5-replacement-filter', 'air_purifier', 'honeywell air genius 5 replacement filter', 'HFD320', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Verify the specific model sticker on your Honeywell Air Genius 5 unit to ensure it requires the HFD320 filter, as listings also reference other codes like HFD300, HFD310, and HFD360 for the broader 3-6 series. Cross-referencing your exact part number prevents ordering incompatible filters for variant models.', '[{"q": "What is the correct replacement filter part number for the Honeywell Air Genius 5?", "a": "The correct replacement filter part number is HFD320. This filter is explicitly listed as compatible with the Honeywell Air Genius 3, 4, 5, and 6 series air purifiers."}, {"q": "Are there differences between OEM and third-party HFD320 filters?", "a": "The provided listings primarily feature third-party replacements, such as multi-packs containing 2 HEPA and 4 activated carbon filters. While OEM status is not confirmed in these specific titles, third-party options often offer value through bundled quantities."}, {"q": "What filtration features are mentioned for the HFD320 filter?", "a": "The listings specify that the HFD320 filter includes HEPA and activated carbon filtration elements. One listing details a multi-pack configuration with 2 HEPA filters and 4 activated carbon filters."}]', 'The Honeywell Air Genius 5 utilizes the HFD320 replacement filter, which is compatible with the Air Genius 3, 4, 5, and 6 series. While specific HEPA grades are not explicitly detailed in the provided listings, the HFD320 is the standard part number for this device. Both OEM and third-party replacement options are available, including multi-pack configurations containing HEPA and activated carbon filters for extended maintenance cycles.', '["The HFD320 is the primary replacement filter code identified for the Honeywell Air Genius 5, sharing compatibility with the Air Genius 3, 4, and 6 series.", "Listings indicate filtration components include HEPA and activated carbon elements, with some third-party options offering multi-packs (e.g., 2x HEPA, 4x Carbon).", "Buyers can choose between single-unit replacements and value multi-packs, with third-party options often providing higher review counts and bundled filter sets."]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO devices (brand_id, model_name, slug, category, seed_keyword, official_filter_code, hepa_grade, filter_shape, dimensions_json, compatibility_warning, faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json, status) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM brands WHERE slug = 'honeywell'), '5 Cabinet', 'honeywell-5-cabinet-replacement-filter', 'air_purifier', 'honeywell 5 filter cabinet', 'FC100A1037', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Buyers should confirm the exact filter part number printed on their Honeywell 5 Cabinet unit, as listings include variants such as FC100A1037, X6670, and other compatible codes. Mismatched dimensions or part codes can lead to improper fit.', '[{"q": "What is the official replacement filter part number for the Honeywell 5 Cabinet air purifier?", "a": "The OEM part is FC100A1037, a 20 × 25 in rectangular filter rated MERV‑11."}, {"q": "Can I use non‑Honeywell filters like Lennox or Nordic Pure for the 5 Cabinet?", "a": "Yes, third‑party filters such as Lennox X6670 (3‑pack) and Nordic Pure (2‑pack) are marketed as compatible, but they are not OEM and may have different dimensions or ratings."}, {"q": "What filtration grades are available for replacements and how do they differ?", "a": "Listings show MERV‑11 (OEM), MERV‑12 (Nordic Pure) and MERV‑16 (Upgrade X7935) options; higher MERV numbers capture smaller particles but may affect airflow."}]', 'The Honeywell 5 Cabinet air purifier uses the official FC100A1037 replacement filter, a 20 × 25 in rectangular unit rated MERV‑11 for particle capture. In addition to this OEM part, compatible third‑party filters such as Lennox X6670 (3‑pack) and Nordic Pure (2‑pack) are sold, offering alternative sizing and value options.', '["Official OEM filter code FC100A1037 (20×25 in) with MERV‑11 rating fits the Honeywell 5 Cabinet.", "Third‑party replacements (e.g., Lennox X6670, Nordic Pure) provide multi‑pack options and similar dimensions.", "Filtration grades range from MERV‑11 to MERV‑12/16, but verify exact model compatibility before purchase."]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO devices (brand_id, model_name, slug, category, seed_keyword, official_filter_code, hepa_grade, filter_shape, dimensions_json, compatibility_warning, faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json, status) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM brands WHERE slug = 'honeywell'), 'Genius 5', 'honeywell-genius-5-replacement-filter', 'air_purifier', 'honeywell genius 5 filter', 'HFD320', 'H13 True HEPA', NULL, NULL, 'Verify your specific Honeywell Genius 5 model sticker to ensure it requires the HFD320 filter, as listings also reference other part numbers like HFD300 and HFD310 for different series. Do not assume cross-compatibility with filters designated for other Honeywell models not listed in the HFD320 series.', '[{"q": "What is the correct replacement filter part number for the Honeywell Air Genius 5?", "a": "Based on the product listings, the HFD320 is the replacement filter part number compatible with the Honeywell Air Genius 5, as well as the Air Genius 3, 4, and 6 series."}, {"q": "Are the listed filters original equipment manufacturer (OEM) parts from Honeywell?", "a": "No, the provided listings are for third-party replacement filters. The titles describe them as ''Replacement Filter'' or ''Compatible with'' Honeywell models, rather than identifying them as genuine Honeywell OEM products."}, {"q": "What filtration grade is associated with the HFD320 filter in these listings?", "a": "One listing explicitly describes the compatible filter as ''H13 True HEPA,'' indicating a high-efficiency filtration standard for capturing fine particles."}]', 'The Honeywell Air Genius 5 utilizes the HFD320 replacement filter, which is compatible with the Air Genius 3, 4, 5, and 6 series. Listings indicate H13 True HEPA filtration capabilities for compatible units. Both single-unit third-party replacements and multi-pack options are available on the market, providing consumers with various purchasing choices for maintaining their air purifier.', '["The HFD320 filter is explicitly listed as compatible with the Honeywell Air Genius 5, alongside models 3, 4, and 6.", "One listing specifies H13 True HEPA filtration for the compatible filter series, indicating high-efficiency particulate capture.", "Consumers can choose between single third-party replacements and 2-pack value options, with no OEM Honeywell-branded filters present in the provided listings."]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO devices (brand_id, model_name, slug, category, seed_keyword, official_filter_code, hepa_grade, filter_shape, dimensions_json, compatibility_warning, faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json, status) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM brands WHERE slug = 'honeywell'), 'Pure 5', 'honeywell-pure-5-replacement-filter', 'air_purifier', 'honeywell pure 5 filter', NULL, NULL, 'rectangular', NULL, 'Verify the exact model sticker and part number on your Honeywell Pure 5 unit, as listings indicate compatibility with Honeywell/Lennox systems and specific dimensions like 16x25x5 or 20x25x5 inches. Do not assume fit without confirming the physical measurements match your device''s filter slot.', '[{"q": "What is the official filter part code for the Honeywell Pure 5?", "a": "The provided listings do not explicitly state an official Honeywell filter part code. They list third-party replacements by Nordic Pure with dimensions such as 16x25x5 and 20x25x5 inches."}, {"q": "Are the listed filters OEM or third-party replacements?", "a": "The listed products are third-party replacements manufactured by Nordic Pure. They are not OEM Honeywell parts, though they are marketed as compatible with Honeywell and Lennox systems."}, {"q": "What filtration grades are available for these replacement filters?", "a": "The listings show filters with MERV 8 and MERV 12 filtration grades. No HEPA grade is explicitly mentioned in the product titles."}]', 'Replacement filters for the Honeywell Pure 5 are available in MERV 8 and MERV 12 grades. While specific official part codes are not listed in the provided data, third-party options like Nordic Pure offer rectangular filters in dimensions such as 16x25x5 and 20x25x5 inches. Buyers can choose between single packs or value two-packs, ensuring compatibility by verifying the exact model sticker on their device before purchase.', '["Listed filters are third-party replacements (Nordic Pure) compatible with Honeywell/Lennox systems, not OEM Honeywell parts.", "Available filtration grades include MERV 8 and MERV 12, with no HEPA grade explicitly stated in the titles.", "Products are sold in single or two-pack configurations with rectangular shapes and dimensions like 16x25x5 or 20x25x5 inches."]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO devices (brand_id, model_name, slug, category, seed_keyword, official_filter_code, hepa_grade, filter_shape, dimensions_json, compatibility_warning, faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json, status) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM brands WHERE slug = 'honeywell'), 'Fpr 7 Air 16X25X1', 'honeywell-fpr-7-air-16x25x1-replacement-filter', 'air_purifier', 'honeywell fpr 7 air filter 16x25x1', NULL, NULL, 'rectangular', '{"length_in": 16, "width_in": 25, "height_in": 1}', 'Verify your specific Honeywell Fpr 7 Air 16X25X1 model sticker to confirm the required MERV rating, as listings show variations between MERV 8, 11, and 13. Note that third-party filters may have slightly smaller actual dimensions (e.g., 15.75"x24.75") compared to the nominal 16x25x1 size.', '[{"q": "What is the correct filter size for the Honeywell Fpr 7 Air 16X25X1?", "a": "The correct nominal size is 16x25x1 inches. While third-party filters like the Simply brand list actual dimensions of 15.75\"x24.75\"x0.75\", they are marketed as compatible with the 16x25x1 specification."}, {"q": "Are there OEM Honeywell filters available for this model?", "a": "Yes, Honeywell offers OEM 4-packs in MERV 11 (Allergen Reducer 11000) and MERV 13 (Allergen Control 13000) grades. Third-party alternatives are also available in MERV 8."}, {"q": "What filtration features do the available 16x25x1 filters offer?", "a": "Listings indicate features include dust, pet, and allergy control for MERV 8 filters, and allergen reduction or control for MERV 11 and MERV 13 Honeywell filters."}]', 'The Honeywell Fpr 7 Air 16X25X1 utilizes a 16x25x1 inch rectangular filter. Available options include Honeywell OEM MERV 11 and MERV 13 filters, as well as third-party MERV 8 replacements. Both single-brand and multi-pack configurations are available for this specific size, ensuring compatibility with standard HVAC systems requiring this dimension.', '["Compatible filters are 16x25x1 inches, with actual dimensions potentially varying slightly (e.g., 15.75\"x24.75\") for third-party brands.", "Filtration grades range from MERV 8 (dust/pet control) to MERV 11 and MERV 13 (allergen reduction/control).", "Buyers can choose between Honeywell OEM 4-packs or third-party value packs (4 or 6 units) from brands like Simply and Filterbuy."]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO devices (brand_id, model_name, slug, category, seed_keyword, official_filter_code, hepa_grade, filter_shape, dimensions_json, compatibility_warning, faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json, status) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM brands WHERE slug = 'honeywell'), 'Fpr 7 Air 20X25X1', 'honeywell-fpr-7-air-20x25x1-replacement-filter', 'air_purifier', 'honeywell fpr 7 air filter 20x25x1', NULL, NULL, 'rectangular', '{"length_in": 20, "width_in": 25, "height_in": 1}', 'Verify that your specific Honeywell Fpr 7 Air unit requires a 20x25x1 inch filter by checking the model sticker, as dimensions vary across different air purifier models. Ensure the MERV rating matches your specific filtration needs, as MERV 8 and MERV 11 offer different levels of particle capture.', '[{"q": "What is the exact filter size for the Honeywell Fpr 7 Air 20X25X1?", "a": "The filter size is 20 inches in length, 25 inches in width, and 1 inch in height, as indicated by the 20x25x1 designation in compatible product listings."}, {"q": "Is the Honeywell 11000 filter the only option for this model?", "a": "No, while the Honeywell 11000 MERV 11 filter is an OEM option, third-party replacements such as Filtrete MERV 11, Aerostar MERV 11, and Filterbuy MERV 8 are also compatible based on the 20x25x1 dimensions."}, {"q": "What is the difference between MERV 8 and MERV 11 filters for this unit?", "a": "MERV 8 filters, like the Filterbuy option, provide basic dust and allergy defense, while MERV 11 filters, such as the Honeywell 11000 and Filtrete options, offer higher efficiency for reducing smaller allergens and particles."}]', 'The Honeywell Fpr 7 Air 20X25X1 utilizes a 20x25x1 inch rectangular filter. Available options include MERV 8 and MERV 11 filtration grades. While no specific official Honeywell part code is explicitly listed in the provided data, both OEM Honeywell 11000 series filters and third-party replacements from brands like Filtrete and Aerostar are available in multi-packs.', '["Compatible filters are rectangular with dimensions of 20 inches by 25 inches by 1 inch.", "Filtration options range from MERV 8 for basic dust defense to MERV 11 for enhanced allergen reduction.", "Buyers can choose between OEM Honeywell 4-packs and third-party value packs from brands such as Filtrete and Aerostar."]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO devices (brand_id, model_name, slug, category, seed_keyword, official_filter_code, hepa_grade, filter_shape, dimensions_json, compatibility_warning, faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json, status) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM brands WHERE slug = 'honeywell'), 'Fpr 7 Air 16X20X1', 'honeywell-fpr-7-air-16x20x1-replacement-filter', 'air_purifier', 'honeywell fpr 7 air filter 16x20x1', NULL, NULL, 'rectangular', '{"length_in": 16, "width_in": 20, "height_in": 1}', 'Buyers should verify the exact model sticker or part number on their Honeywell FPR 7 unit, as some listings use generic dimensions or different MERV ratings that may not meet specific performance needs.', '[{"q": "What part number or code should I look for when buying a replacement filter for the Honeywell FPR 7 Air 16x20x1?", "a": "The listings do not provide a specific official part code; you need a 16×20×1 in rectangular filter that matches the FPR 7 model."}, {"q": "Is there a difference between Honeywell OEM filters and the third‑party packs shown?", "a": "Honeywell OEM filters are branded and listed with MERV 11, while third‑party packs are unbranded, typically MERV 8, and sold in larger quantities."}, {"q": "What filtration grades are available for this size filter and how often should they be replaced?", "a": "Available grades in the listings range from MERV 8 to MERV 11; replacement frequency depends on usage but generally every 3‑6 months for typical residential use."}]', 'The Honeywell FPR 7 Air 16x20x1 uses a 16×20×1‑inch rectangular filter; no specific part code is listed in the titles. Replacement options include Honeywell OEM filters and third‑party multi‑pack filters with MERV 8‑11 ratings. These filters are available in packs of two to six and provide allergen reduction for residential HVAC systems.', '["OEM Honeywell filter and third‑party packs both match the 16×20×1 in rectangular size required for the FPR 7.", "Listings show MERV 11 (Honeywell) and MERV 8 filters, indicating varying filtration efficiency.", "Multi‑pack options (2‑6 units) offer value, while OEM provides brand assurance."]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO devices (brand_id, model_name, slug, category, seed_keyword, official_filter_code, hepa_grade, filter_shape, dimensions_json, compatibility_warning, faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json, status) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM brands WHERE slug = 'honeywell'), 'Fpr 7 Air 20X30X1', 'honeywell-fpr-7-air-20x30x1-replacement-filter', 'air_purifier', 'honeywell fpr 7 air filter 20x30x1', NULL, NULL, 'rectangular', '{"length_in": 20, "width_in": 30, "height_in": 1}', 'Verify your specific Honeywell Fpr 7 Air 20X30X1 model sticker to confirm the 20x30x1 dimension requirement. Note that third-party filters may have slightly smaller actual dimensions (e.g., 19.94"x29.94") to ensure proper fit.', '[{"q": "What is the exact filter size for the Honeywell Fpr 7 Air 20X30X1?", "a": "The required filter size is 20x30x1 inches. Some third-party listings specify actual dimensions of 19.94\"x29.94\"x0.75\" to accommodate frame fit."}, {"q": "Is the Honeywell 11000 filter the same as the Fpr 7 Air 20X30X1 filter?", "a": "The Honeywell 11000 is a MERV 11 filter in a 20x30x1 size, which matches the dimensions and filtration grade indicated for the Fpr 7 Air 20X30X1."}, {"q": "What filtration levels are available for this filter size?", "a": "Listings show options for MERV 8 (dust, pet, and allergy control) and MERV 11 (allergen reducer, comparable to MPR 1200)."}]', 'The Honeywell Fpr 7 Air 20X30X1 utilizes a 20x30x1 inch rectangular filter. Listings indicate compatibility with MERV 8 and MERV 11 filtration grades, including options comparable to MPR 1200. Both official Honeywell 4-packs and third-party value packs are available for this specific size and filtration standard.', '["Compatible filters are 20x30x1 inches, with actual dimensions often measuring 19.94\"x29.94\"x0.75\".", "Available filtration grades include MERV 8 for dust/pet control and MERV 11 for allergen reduction.", "Options range from official Honeywell 4-packs to third-party 2-pack and 6-pack value sets."]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO devices (brand_id, model_name, slug, category, seed_keyword, official_filter_code, hepa_grade, filter_shape, dimensions_json, compatibility_warning, faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json, status) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM brands WHERE slug = 'honeywell'), 'Fpr 7 Air 14X25X1', 'honeywell-fpr-7-air-14x25x1-replacement-filter', 'air_purifier', 'honeywell fpr 7 air filter 14x25x1', NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"length_in": 13.75, "width_in": 24.75, "height_in": 0.75}', 'Before purchasing, confirm the exact Honeywell Fpr 7 Air model sticker or part number, as some listings reference 14×25×1 filters that may not match all Fpr 7 variants.', '[{"q": "What filter part code is compatible with the Honeywell Fpr 7 Air 14X25X1?", "a": "The listings do not specify an official Honeywell part code; the unit uses a 14×25×1 filter size."}, {"q": "Are Honeywell filters OEM for the Fpr 7 Air?", "a": "Yes, Honeywell’s own 14×25×1 MERV 11 filter is an OEM replacement, while other brands offer third‑party options."}, {"q": "What filtration grades are available for this unit?", "a": "Available filters include MERV 11 from Honeywell, Filtrete, and Aerostar, and MERV 8 from Simply, all sized 14×25×1."}]', 'The Honeywell Fpr 7 Air 14X25X1 accepts 14×25×1 air filters. MERV 11 filters are common, with Honeywell’s own 14x25x1 MERV 11 filter available. Third‑party brands also offer 14×25×1 MERV 11 or MERV 8 options in multi‑pack bundles. Both OEM and value packs fit the unit.', '["Compatible 14×25×1 filters fit the Honeywell Fpr 7 Air", "MERV 11 and MERV 8 grades are available from Honeywell and third‑party brands", "OEM Honeywell filters and multi‑pack third‑party options are both offered"]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO devices (brand_id, model_name, slug, category, seed_keyword, official_filter_code, hepa_grade, filter_shape, dimensions_json, compatibility_warning, faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json, status) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM brands WHERE slug = 'honeywell'), 'Merv 8', 'honeywell-merv-8-replacement-filter', 'air_purifier', 'honeywell merv 8 filter', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Verify the exact dimensions and part number on your existing filter or unit sticker, as listings show varying sizes such as 16x25x4 and 20x25x5. Do not assume a single part number fits all Honeywell Merv 8 models without checking specific compatibility.', '[{"q": "What is the official part number for Honeywell Merv 8 filters?", "a": "The provided listings do not explicitly state a single official Honeywell part number for the Merv 8 filter. One third-party listing references compatibility with Honeywell FC100A1037, but this is not confirmed as the universal OEM code for all Merv 8 units."}, {"q": "Are third-party Merv 8 filters compatible with Honeywell systems?", "a": "Yes, listings show third-party brands like AIRx and Nordic Pure offering Merv 8 filters that fit Honeywell systems. For example, AIRx filters are listed as fitting Honeywell FC100A1037, and Nordic Pure offers Honeywell/Lennox replacements."}, {"q": "What filtration grade do these Honeywell Merv 8 filters provide?", "a": "All listed products specify a MERV 8 filtration grade. This rating indicates the filter''s ability to capture fine particles, though no HEPA grade is mentioned in the titles."}]', 'Replacement filters for the Honeywell Merv 8 include OEM Honeywell Home units and third-party alternatives like AIRx and Nordic Pure. Listings specify MERV 8 filtration grade but do not provide a single universal official part code. Available dimensions vary by listing, including 16x25x4 and 20x25x5 inches. Buyers should verify their specific unit''s required size and part number to ensure compatibility with their Honeywell air purifier or furnace system.', '["Listings confirm MERV 8 filtration grade for both OEM Honeywell Home and third-party brands like AIRx and Nordic Pure.", "Dimensions vary across products, with specific sizes including 16x25x4 inches and 20x25x5 inches, requiring precise measurement for fit.", "OEM Honeywell Home filters are sold in 3-packs, while third-party options offer 2-packs or 3-packs, providing different value propositions."]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO devices (brand_id, model_name, slug, category, seed_keyword, official_filter_code, hepa_grade, filter_shape, dimensions_json, compatibility_warning, faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json, status) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM brands WHERE slug = 'honeywell'), 'Fpr 9 Air 20X20X1', 'honeywell-fpr-9-air-20x20x1-replacement-filter', 'air_purifier', 'honeywell fpr 9 air filter 20x20x1', NULL, NULL, 'rectangular', '{"length_in": 20, "width_in": 20, "height_in": 1}', 'Verify the exact model sticker or part number on your Honeywell FPR9 Air unit before purchasing, as some listings use generic 20 × 20 × 1 dimensions that may not match variant-specific codes.', '[{"q": "What part number should I look for when ordering a replacement filter for the Honeywell FPR9 Air?", "a": "The listings do not provide a specific Honeywell part number; the filter is identified by its 20 × 20 × 1‑inch size, so check the model sticker for the official code before buying."}, {"q": "Is there a benefit to buying the OEM Honeywell filter versus third‑party options?", "a": "OEM filters guarantee the exact Honeywell specifications and fit, while third‑party packs offer lower cost and larger quantities but may lack the official part code."}, {"q": "What filtration grades are available for this size filter?", "a": "Available grades in the current listings range from MERV 8 (basic dust protection) to MERV 11 (enhanced allergen and pet dander capture)."}]', 'Replacement filters for the Honeywell FPR9 Air model are 20 × 20 × 1‑inch rectangular units. No specific Honeywell part number is listed in the available titles, and filtration grades range from MERV 8 to MERV 11. Both OEM Honeywell filters and multi‑pack widely available third‑party options are readily sold today.', '["All listed filters share the 20 × 20 × 1‑inch rectangular size required for the Honeywell FPR9 Air.", "Filtration performance varies, with MERV 8 (Filterbuy) and MERV 11 (Honeywell, BNX, Amazon Basics) options.", "Buyers can choose OEM Honeywell packs (4‑pack) or larger value multi‑packs from third‑party brands."]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO devices (brand_id, model_name, slug, category, seed_keyword, official_filter_code, hepa_grade, filter_shape, dimensions_json, compatibility_warning, faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json, status) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM brands WHERE slug = 'honeywell'), 'Fpr 9 Air 16X20X1', 'honeywell-fpr-9-air-16x20x1-replacement-filter', 'air_purifier', 'honeywell fpr 9 air filter 16x20x1', NULL, NULL, 'rectangular', '{"length_in": 16, "width_in": 20, "height_in": 1}', 'Verify the exact model sticker on your Honeywell Fpr 9 Air unit to confirm the 16x20x1 dimension requirement. Note that while dimensions match, filtration efficiency varies significantly between MERV 8, 11, and 13 options, so select the grade appropriate for your air quality needs.', '[{"q": "What is the official filter part code for the Honeywell Fpr 9 Air 16X20X1?", "a": "The scraped listings do not explicitly state a single official part code for the Fpr 9 Air model itself, but they list compatible Honeywell filters such as the Allergen Reducer 11000 and Allergen Control 13000 in 16x20x1 sizes."}, {"q": "What is the difference between the Honeywell OEM filters and third-party options like Filtrete?", "a": "Honeywell OEM filters include the MERV 11 Allergen Reducer and MERV 13 Allergen Control, both sold in 4-packs. Filtrete offers a MERV 11 option in a 2-pack, while Amazon Basics provides a MERV 8 option in a 6-pack, offering different filtration levels and pack sizes."}, {"q": "What filtration features are available for this filter size?", "a": "Listings show options for MERV 8 (removes dust, lint, pollen), MERV 11 (allergen reduction, MPR 1000), and MERV 13 (allergen control). The specific features depend on the MERV rating selected from the available products."}]', 'The Honeywell Fpr 9 Air 16X20X1 utilizes 16x20x1 rectangular air filters. Available options include Honeywell Allergen Reducer MERV 11 and Allergen Control MERV 13 models. Third-party replacements like Filtrete MERV 11 and Amazon Basics MERV 8 are also compatible. Buyers can select between OEM single or multi-packs and value-oriented third-party 4-packs or 6-packs based on filtration needs.', '["Compatible filters are 16x20x1 rectangular units, with MERV 8, MERV 11, and MERV 13 filtration grades available in the listings.", "Honeywell offers OEM options including the Allergen Reducer 11000 (MERV 11) and Allergen Control 13000 (MERV 13) in 4-packs.", "Third-party alternatives include Filtrete MERV 11 (2-pack) and Amazon Basics MERV 8 (6-pack), providing varied cost and quantity options."]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO devices (brand_id, model_name, slug, category, seed_keyword, official_filter_code, hepa_grade, filter_shape, dimensions_json, compatibility_warning, faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json, status) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM brands WHERE slug = 'honeywell'), 'Fpr 9 Air 14X25X1', 'honeywell-fpr-9-air-14x25x1-replacement-filter', 'air_purifier', 'honeywell fpr 9 air filter 14x25x1', NULL, NULL, 'rectangular', '{"length_in": 14, "width_in": 25, "height_in": 1}', 'Verify the exact model sticker on your Honeywell Fpr 9 Air 14X25X1 unit to confirm the 14x25x1 dimension requirement. Note that some third-party listings indicate actual sizes may vary slightly (e.g., 13.75"x24.75"), so check specific product details before ordering.', '[{"q": "What is the correct filter size for the Honeywell Fpr 9 Air 14X25X1?", "a": "The correct filter size is 14x25x1 inches, as indicated by the model number and confirmed by multiple compatible product listings."}, {"q": "Are there OEM and third-party options for this filter?", "a": "Yes, the Honeywell 11000 is an OEM option, while third-party brands like Filterbuy, Filtrete, and Simply offer compatible replacements in various pack sizes."}, {"q": "What filtration ratings are available for this model?", "a": "Listings show options for MERV 8 (dust and allergy defense) and MERV 11 (allergen reducer) filtration grades."}]', 'The Honeywell Fpr 9 Air 14X25X1 utilizes a 14x25x1 rectangular filter. While no specific official part code is listed in the provided data, compatible replacements include MERV 8 and MERV 11 grades. Both OEM Honeywell units and third-party multi-packs from brands like Filterbuy and Filtrete are available for this specific dimension and filtration standard.', '["Compatible filters for the Honeywell Fpr 9 Air 14X25X1 measure 14x25x1 inches.", "Available filtration grades in the listings include MERV 8 and MERV 11 for dust and allergy control.", "Buyers can choose between OEM Honeywell 4-packs and third-party value packs from brands like Filterbuy and Filtrete."]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO devices (brand_id, model_name, slug, category, seed_keyword, official_filter_code, hepa_grade, filter_shape, dimensions_json, compatibility_warning, faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json, status) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM brands WHERE slug = 'blueair'), 'Blue Pure 211', 'blueair-blue-pure-211-replacement-filter', 'air_purifier', 'blueair replacement filter for blue pure 211', NULL, 'H13', NULL, NULL, 'Buyers must verify their exact model sticker, as listings distinguish between the 211+, 211+ Auto, and 211i Max variants. Filters for the 211i Max may not be interchangeable with standard 211+ models without confirming specific part numbers.', '[{"q": "What is the official filter part code for the Blueair Blue Pure 211?", "a": "The provided product listings do not explicitly state an official filter part code. They identify compatibility with the 211+ and 211i Max series but do not list specific alphanumeric part numbers."}, {"q": "What is the difference between OEM and third-party filters for this model?", "a": "OEM filters are labeled as ''Genuine'' by Blueair for specific models like the 211+ Auto and 211i Max. Third-party options, such as the 2-pack for the 211+ series, are compatible replacements that may offer lower cost per unit but are not manufactured by Blueair."}, {"q": "What filtration features do these replacement filters provide?", "a": "The filters utilize a 2-stage filtration system consisting of H13 True HEPA and activated carbon. This combination is designed to capture fine particulates and reduce odors in the Blue Pure 211 series air purifiers."}]', 'The Blueair Blue Pure 211 series utilizes a 2-stage filtration system featuring H13 True HEPA and activated carbon media. While specific official part codes are not explicitly listed in the provided data, genuine OEM filters are available for the 211+ and 211i Max variants. Third-party options include 2-pack replacements compatible with the 211+ series, offering cost-effective alternatives for maintaining air quality.', '["Listings confirm compatibility with Blue Pure 211+ and 211i Max models, featuring a 2-stage H13 True HEPA and activated carbon filtration system.", "OEM genuine filters are available for specific variants like the 211+ Auto and 211i Max, ensuring exact manufacturer specifications.", "Third-party 2-pack replacements are available for the 211+ series, providing a multi-unit option for users seeking value over single-unit OEM purchases."]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO devices (brand_id, model_name, slug, category, seed_keyword, official_filter_code, hepa_grade, filter_shape, dimensions_json, compatibility_warning, faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json, status) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM brands WHERE slug = 'blueair'), '211I', 'blueair-211i-replacement-filter', 'air_purifier', 'blueair 211i hepa filter', NULL, 'H13', NULL, NULL, 'Before purchasing, confirm your Blueair 211I unit’s exact model sticker or part number, as some listings reference the 211i Max variant and may not match all 211I configurations.', '[{"q": "What part code should I look for to ensure compatibility with my Blueair 211I?", "a": "Look for the replacement part number F2MAX, which is listed in several third‑party filters and is compatible with the Blueair 211i Max series."}, {"q": "How do OEM Genuine filters differ from third‑party AllergenBlock replacements?", "a": "OEM Genuine filters are manufactured by Blueair and carry the brand name, while third‑party AllergenBlock replacements are produced by other manufacturers and may not carry the Blueair logo."}, {"q": "What filtration features are available in the replacement filters for the Blueair 211I?", "a": "Replacement filters include H13 True HEPA filtration and high‑efficiency activated carbon, providing allergen and odor reduction."}]', 'Replacement filters for the Blueair 211I include OEM Genuine filters and third‑party AllergenBlock options. The H13 True HEPA grade appears in some listings, such as the F2MAX part. Both single‑piece OEM filters and multi‑pack third‑party replacements are available, offering flexibility for households today.', '["All listed filters are compatible with the Blueair 211I/211i Max series.", "The H13 True HEPA grade is present in the F2MAX replacement part.", "OEM Genuine filters and third‑party multi‑pack options are both available."]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO devices (brand_id, model_name, slug, category, seed_keyword, official_filter_code, hepa_grade, filter_shape, dimensions_json, compatibility_warning, faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json, status) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM brands WHERE slug = 'blueair'), '311', 'blueair-311-replacement-filter', 'air_purifier', 'blueair 311 hepa filter', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Verify the exact model number on your Blueair unit''s sticker or part label before ordering, as some listings reference the 311 Auto or 311i Max variants which may differ from your specific device.', '[{"q": "What is the part code for a Blueair 311 replacement filter?", "a": "The product titles do not include a specific part number; check your unit’s model sticker or Blueair documentation for the correct code."}, {"q": "Are OEM filters different from third‑party multi‑pack replacements?", "a": "OEM filters are labeled “Genuine” and are made by Blueair, while third‑party listings are multi‑pack replacements without the genuine branding."}, {"q": "What filtration features do these filters have?", "a": "One OEM listing mentions an AllergenBlock feature, but none provide an explicit HEPA grade or shape; performance details should be confirmed with the manufacturer."}]', 'Replacement filters compatible with the Blueair 311 are sold as genuine Blueair units and as third‑party multi‑pack options. No specific filter part code or HEPA grade is listed in the titles, but OEM filters are labeled “Genuine” while other listings offer two‑pack replacements for customers.', '["Genuine Blueair and third‑party filters are both listed as compatible with the Blueair 311 (including 311 Auto and 311i Max variants).", "The titles provide no explicit HEPA grade, filter shape, or dimensions; one OEM filter mentions an AllergenBlock feature.", "Buyers can choose single OEM filters or value‑packed multi‑pack third‑party replacements."]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO devices (brand_id, model_name, slug, category, seed_keyword, official_filter_code, hepa_grade, filter_shape, dimensions_json, compatibility_warning, faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json, status) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM brands WHERE slug = 'blueair'), 'Purifier 411', 'blueair-purifier-411-replacement-filter', 'air_purifier', 'blueair purifier filter 411', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Verify your specific unit is a Blueair 411, 411+, or 411 Auto, as listings distinguish these variants from the 411i Max and 411a Max models. Do not assume cross-compatibility with Max series filters without checking the model sticker.', '[{"q": "What filter part code fits the Blueair Purifier 411?", "a": "The provided listings do not explicitly state a specific alphanumeric part code, but confirm compatibility with the 411, 411+, and 411 Auto series."}, {"q": "Is the Blue Pure filter an OEM replacement for the Blueair 411?", "a": "No, the Blue Pure filter is a third-party replacement, whereas the ''BLUEAIR Genuine'' filter is the OEM option."}, {"q": "What filtration features are specified for the Blueair 411 filter?", "a": "The listings mention ''Everyday'' filtration for the genuine filter but do not specify HEPA grades or other technical filtration metrics in the titles."}]', 'The Blueair Purifier 411 utilizes replacement filters compatible with the 411, 411+, and 411 Auto models. Listings indicate availability of genuine Blueair filters and third-party replacements from Blue Pure. Specific filtration grades and official part codes are not explicitly detailed in the provided product titles. Buyers can select between single OEM units or multi-pack third-party options for maintenance.', '["Filters are explicitly compatible with Blueair 411, 411+, and 411 Auto air purifier models.", "Both genuine Blueair OEM filters and third-party Blue Pure replacements are available in the market.", "Specific HEPA grades and physical dimensions are not stated in the provided product titles."]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO devices (brand_id, model_name, slug, category, seed_keyword, official_filter_code, hepa_grade, filter_shape, dimensions_json, compatibility_warning, faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json, status) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM brands WHERE slug = 'blueair'), '2 In 1', 'blueair-2-in-1-replacement-filter', 'air_purifier', 'blueair 2 in 1 replacement filter', 'DH3i', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Verify that your specific Blueair 2 In 1 unit is labeled for the DH3i filter system, as the listings specify compatibility with the ''Purify + Humidify'' variant. Ensure the model sticker matches the DH3i designation to avoid ordering incompatible filters for other Blueair models.', '[{"q": "What is the correct filter part number for the Blueair 2 In 1?", "a": "The correct filter part number is DH3i, which is explicitly cited in the titles of both OEM and third-party replacement listings for the Blueair 2 In 1 Purify + Humidify air purifier."}, {"q": "Is there a difference between OEM and third-party filters for this model?", "a": "Yes, OEM filters are manufactured by Blueair and are labeled as ''Genuine,'' while third-party options are labeled as ''Compatible'' or ''Replacement.'' Third-party listings often offer multi-packs containing both particle and wick filters, whereas the OEM listing specifically highlights the wick filter."}, {"q": "What filtration features do the DH3i filters provide?", "a": "The DH3i filters are designed for dual functionality, capturing water minerals and delivering pure water humidification in addition to standard air purification. The system utilizes separate particle filters and wick filters to maintain both air quality and humidity levels."}]', 'The Blueair 2 In 1 air purifier utilizes the DH3i filter system, which includes both particle and wick components for combined purification and humidification. While specific HEPA grades are not explicitly detailed in the provided listings, the DH3i code is the primary identifier for compatibility. Both genuine OEM wick filters and third-party multi-pack replacements containing particle and wick elements are available for this model.', '["The DH3i filter code is the specific identifier for replacement filters compatible with the Blueair 2 In 1 Purify + Humidify unit.", "Filtration systems for this model include distinct particle filters and wick filters designed to capture water minerals and deliver pure water humidification.", "Consumers can choose between genuine Blueair OEM wick filters and third-party value packs that bundle multiple particle filters with wick replacements."]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO devices (brand_id, model_name, slug, category, seed_keyword, official_filter_code, hepa_grade, filter_shape, dimensions_json, compatibility_warning, faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json, status) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM brands WHERE slug = 'blueair'), '3 In 1', 'blueair-3-in-1-replacement-filter', 'air_purifier', 'blueair 3 in 1 filter', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Verify your exact Blueair 3 In 1 model sticker, as listings distinguish between the T10i and DH3i variants. Filters for the DH3i 2-in-1 Purify + Humidify may not be compatible with other 3-in-1 models.', '[{"q": "What is the official filter part code for the Blueair 3 In 1?", "a": "The provided listings do not explicitly state a universal official filter part code for the Blueair 3 In 1. They identify compatibility for the T10i model and the DH3i model, suggesting distinct filter requirements for different variants."}, {"q": "Are there OEM and third-party options for Blueair 3 In 1 filters?", "a": "Yes, the listings include a genuine Blueair filter for the DH3i and a replacement filter for the T10i. Additionally, third-party multi-packs containing particle and wick filters are available for the DH3i variant."}, {"q": "What filtration features are highlighted for these filters?", "a": "The titles mention ''Pure Water Humidification'' and ''Capture Water Minerals'' for the DH3i wick filter, as well as general ''Particle Filters'' in third-party packs. Specific HEPA grades are not listed in the provided data."}]', 'The Blueair 3 In 1 air purifier utilizes a replacement filter system, with specific listings identifying compatibility for the T10i variant. While the provided data does not specify a universal official part code or HEPA grade for the entire 3 In 1 series, genuine Blueair filters and third-party multi-packs are available. Buyers should verify their specific model number, as listings distinguish between T10i and DH3i units, to ensure correct filtration component selection.', '["Listings confirm replacement filters for the Blueair T10i, a specific variant within the 3-in-1 category, but do not provide a universal part code for all 3 In 1 models.", "Filtration features mentioned include particle filtration and water mineral capture for humidification, though specific HEPA grades are not explicitly stated in the titles.", "Both OEM genuine Blueair filters and third-party multi-packs (e.g., 3 particle + 1 wick) are available, requiring careful model verification to avoid incompatibility with DH3i or other variants."]', 'enriched') ON CONFLICT(slug) DO UPDATE SET official_filter_code=excluded.official_filter_code, hepa_grade=excluded.hepa_grade, filter_shape=excluded.filter_shape, dimensions_json=excluded.dimensions_json, compatibility_warning=excluded.compatibility_warning, faqs_json=excluded.faqs_json, direct_answer_capsule=excluded.direct_answer_capsule, key_takeaways_json=excluded.key_takeaways_json, status=excluded.status, updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
